{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"database-runner","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Database Runner","description":"Run the selected SQL or the statement under the cursor on PostgreSQL or SQLite with the command line client, and read the result in a panel.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:dbRunner.run","onCommand:dbRunner.runFile","onCommand:dbRunner.listTables","onCommand:dbRunner.describeTable","onCommand:dbRunner.previewTable","onCommand:dbRunner.countRows"],"permissions":["terminal","workspace.read","workspace.write"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"dbRunner.run","title":"Run Statement or Selection","category":"Database Runner"},{"command":"dbRunner.runFile","title":"Run the Whole File","category":"Database Runner"},{"command":"dbRunner.listTables","title":"List Tables","category":"Database Runner"},{"command":"dbRunner.describeTable","title":"Describe a Table...","category":"Database Runner"},{"command":"dbRunner.previewTable","title":"Show the First 20 Rows of a Table...","category":"Database Runner"},{"command":"dbRunner.countRows","title":"Count Rows of a Table...","category":"Database Runner"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"dbRunner.run","key":"Ctrl+Alt+Enter"}],"configuration":{"title":"Database Runner","properties":{"dbRunner.engine":{"type":"string","enum":["postgres","sqlite","mysql"],"default":"postgres","description":"The database: postgres (psql), sqlite (sqlite3) or mysql (runs in the terminal)."},"dbRunner.target":{"type":"string","default":"","description":"PostgreSQL: a connection URL such as postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb. SQLite: the path of the database file."},"dbRunner.mysqlArgs":{"type":"string","default":"","description":"MySQL only: the arguments for the mysql command, for example \"-h 127.0.0.1 -u root -p mydb\" (-p asks for the password in the terminal)."},"dbRunner.timeoutSeconds":{"type":"number","default":30,"description":"How long to wait for a result before giving up."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Database Runner: run the SQL you selected (or the statement under the cursor) against PostgreSQL or SQLite using the command line\n// client you already have (psql, sqlite3), and read the result in a panel. For MySQL it runs the query in the terminal.\n// The query is written to .ferrum/db/query.sql and the result is read back from .ferrum/db/out.txt.\n\nconst DIR = '.ferrum/db';\nconst QUERY = DIR + '/query.sql';\nconst OUT = DIR + '/out.txt';\nconst MARK = '__FERRUM_DONE__';\n\n/** The statement that contains the cursor. Statements end at `;`, outside quotes and comments. */\nfunction statementAt(text, offset) {\n  const spans = [];\n  let start = 0;\n  let i = 0;\n  let q = '';\n  while (i < text.length) {\n    const c = text[i];\n    const n = text[i + 1];\n    if (q) {\n      if (c === q) { if (n === q) i++; else q = ''; }\n    } else if (c === \"'\" || c === '\"' || c === '`') q = c;\n    else if (c === '-' && n === '-') { while (i < text.length && text[i] !== '\\n') i++; continue; }\n    else if (c === '/' && n === '*') { const e = text.indexOf('*/', i + 2); i = e < 0 ? text.length : e + 1; }\n    else if (c === '$' && /^\\$[A-Za-z_]*\\$/.test(text.slice(i))) {\n      const tag = /^\\$[A-Za-z_]*\\$/.exec(text.slice(i))[0];\n      const e = text.indexOf(tag, i + tag.length);\n      i = e < 0 ? text.length : e + tag.length - 1;\n    } else if (c === ';') { spans.push([start, i + 1]); start = i + 1; }\n    i++;\n  }\n  if (text.slice(start).trim()) spans.push([start, text.length]);\n  if (!spans.length) return '';\n  let hit = spans.find(([a, b]) => offset >= a && offset <= b);\n  // A cursor on blank space before a statement runs that statement.\n  if (!hit) hit = spans.find(([a]) => offset < a) || spans[spans.length - 1];\n  return text.slice(hit[0], hit[1]).trim();\n}\n\n/** SQL that deletes data or schema, or updates and deletes with no WHERE. The person is asked before it runs. */\nfunction risky(sql) {\n  const s = sql.replace(/--.*$/gm, '').replace(/\\/\\*[\\s\\S]*?\\*\\//g, '');\n  return s.split(';').some((st) => /\\b(drop|truncate|alter)\\b/i.test(st) || (/\\b(delete\\s+from|update)\\b/i.test(st) && !/\\bwhere\\b/i.test(st)));\n}\n\nconst safeTable =(s) => (/^[A-Za-z_][\\w.$]{0,80}$/.test(String(s || '').trim()) ? String(s).trim() : null);\nconst badArg = (s) => /[\"\\n\\r$`]/.test(String(s));\n\n/** The query file and the command for an engine. Returns { file, command, capture }. */\nfunction plan(engine, target, sql, extra = {}) {\n  if (engine === 'postgres') {\n    return {\n      file: sql.replace(/\\s*$/, '\\n') + '\\\\qecho ' + MARK + '\\n',\n      command: `psql \"${target}\" -X -f \"${QUERY}\" -o \"${OUT}\"`,\n      capture: true,\n    };\n  }\n  if (engine === 'sqlite') {\n    return {\n      file: sql.replace(/\\s*$/, '\\n'),\n      command: `sqlite3 \"${target}\" \".headers on\" \".mode column\" \".output ${OUT}\" \".read ${QUERY}\" \".print ${MARK}\" \".output stdout\"`,\n      capture: true,\n    };\n  }\n  return { file: sql.replace(/\\s*$/, '\\n'), command: `mysql ${extra.args || ''} -e \"source ${QUERY}\"`.replace(/\\s+/g, ' '), capture: false };\n}\n\nfunction cleanResult(text) {\n  return String(text).replace(new RegExp(MARK + '\\\\s*$'), '').replace(/\\s+$/, '');\n}\n\nconst esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');\n\nfunction resultPage(sql, out, ms, note) {\n  const lines = out ? out.split('\\n').length : 0;\n  return `<style>\n  body { font-family: var(--ui); } h3 { margin: 0 0 4px; } .dim { color: var(--fg-dim); font-size: 12px; }\n  pre { font: 12.5px/1.55 var(--mono, monospace); background: var(--raised, rgba(128,128,128,.12)); border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px 12px; overflow: auto; margin: 10px 0; white-space: pre; }\n  details { margin-top: 12px; } summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--fg-dim); }\n</style>\n<h3>Result</h3>\n<div class=\"dim\">${esc(note || '')}${ms !== null ? (note ? ' · ' : '') + ms + ' ms' : ''}${lines ? ' · ' + lines + ' line' + (lines === 1 ? '' : 's') : ''}</div>\n<pre>${out ? esc(out) : '(no output: the statement ran and returned nothing)'}</pre>\n<details><summary>The SQL that ran</summary><pre>${esc(sql)}</pre></details>`;\n}\n\nexports._test = { statementAt, plan, cleanResult, safeTable, badArg, risky, MARK };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  let panel = null;\n  const reg = (id, fn) => context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register(id, fn));\n  const setting = (k) => String(ferrum.settings.get('dbRunner.' + k) || '').trim();\n  const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\n\n  async function ensureReady() {\n    if (!ferrum.workspace.root) { ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a folder first; the query files are kept in .ferrum/db.', 'warn'); return null; }\n    const engine = setting('engine') || 'postgres';\n    const target = engine === 'mysql' ? setting('mysqlArgs') : setting('target');\n    if (engine !== 'mysql' && !target) {\n      ferrum.window.showMessage(engine === 'postgres' ? 'Set the connection in the settings: dbRunner.target, for example postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb' : 'Set the SQLite file in the settings: dbRunner.target, for example data/app.sqlite', 'warn');\n      return null;\n    }\n    if (badArg(target)) { ferrum.window.showMessage('The connection has characters I will not put in a command (a quote, $ or a backtick).', 'warn'); return null; }\n    return { engine, target };\n  }\n\n  async function show(html) {\n    if (panel) return panel.setHtml(html);\n    panel = await ferrum.window.showPanel({ title: 'Query result', html });\n    panel.onDidClose(() => (panel = null));\n  }\n\n  async function execute(sql) {\n    const cfg = await ensureReady();\n    if (!cfg) return;\n    if (!sql.trim()) return ferrum.window.showMessage('There is no SQL to run.', 'warn');\n    if (risky(sql) && !(await ferrum.window.confirm('This SQL can destroy data:\\n\\n' + sql.trim().slice(0, 300) + '\\n\\nRun it on ' + (cfg.engine === 'mysql' ? 'your MySQL server' : cfg.target.replace(/\\/\\/[^@/]*@/, '//***@')) + '?', 'Run it'))) return;\n    const p = plan(cfg.engine, cfg.target, sql, { args: cfg.target });\n    await ferrum.workspace.writeFile(QUERY, p.file);\n    if (!p.capture) {\n      await ferrum.terminal.run(p.command);\n      return ferrum.window.showMessage('Running in the terminal. The result of MySQL queries stays there.');\n    }\n    await ferrum.workspace.writeFile(OUT, '');\n    const t0 = Date.now();\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(p.command);\n    const limit = Math.max(5, Number(ferrum.settings.get('dbRunner.timeoutSeconds')) || 30) * 1000;\n    let text = '';\n    while (Date.now() - t0 < limit) {\n      await sleep(450);\n      try { text = await ferrum.workspace.readFile(OUT); } catch { text = ''; }\n      if (text.includes(MARK)) break;\n    }\n    const done = text.includes(MARK);\n    const body = cleanResult(text);\n    await show(resultPage(sql, body, done ? Date.now() - t0 : null, done ? 'Finished' : 'No result after ' + Math.round(limit / 1000) + ' s. Look at the terminal: the query may still be running or have failed.'));\n    if (!done) ferrum.window.showMessage('No result yet. Check the terminal for an error.', 'warn');\n  }\n\n  reg('dbRunner.run', async () => {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a SQL file first.', 'warn');\n    let sql = doc.selectedText;\n    if (!sql) {\n      const lines = doc.text.split('\\n');\n      const { line, col } = doc.selection.start;\n      const offset = lines.slice(0, line).reduce((n, l) => n + l.length + 1, 0) + col;\n      sql = statementAt(doc.text, offset);\n    }\n    await execute(sql);\n  });\n  reg('dbRunner.runFile', async () => {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a SQL file first.', 'warn');\n    await execute(doc.text);\n  });\n  reg('dbRunner.listTables', async () => {\n    const e = setting('engine') || 'postgres';\n    await execute(e === 'sqlite' ? \"SELECT name AS table_name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = 'table' ORDER BY name;\" : e === 'mysql' ? 'SHOW TABLES;' : \"SELECT table_schema, table_name FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema NOT IN ('pg_catalog','information_schema') ORDER BY 1, 2;\");\n  });\n  reg('dbRunner.describeTable', async () => {\n    const t = safeTable(await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Table name' }));\n    if (!t) return;\n    const e = setting('engine') || 'postgres';\n    await execute(e === 'sqlite' ? 'PRAGMA table_info(' + t + ');' : e === 'mysql' ? 'DESCRIBE ' + t + ';' : \"SELECT column_name, data_type, is_nullable, column_default FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = '\" + t.split('.').pop() + \"' ORDER BY ordinal_position;\");\n  });\n  reg('dbRunner.countRows', async () => {\n    const t = safeTable(await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Table name' }));\n    if (t) await execute('SELECT COUNT(*) AS rows FROM ' + t + ';');\n  });\n  reg('dbRunner.previewTable', async () => {\n    const t = safeTable(await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Table name' }));\n    if (t) await execute('SELECT * FROM ' + t + ' LIMIT 20;');\n  });\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Database Runner\n\nSelect some SQL (or just put the cursor in a statement) and press **Ctrl+Alt+Enter**. The query runs with the **client you already have installed**, and the result appears in a panel.\n\n| Engine | Needs | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| PostgreSQL | `psql` on your PATH | In a panel |\n| SQLite | `sqlite3` on your PATH | In a panel |\n| MySQL | `mysql` on your PATH | In the terminal only |\n\n## How it works, honestly\n\nThe extension cannot read the terminal. So it writes your SQL to `.ferrum/db/query.sql`, types the `psql` or `sqlite3` command in the terminal (you see it), and the client writes its output to `.ferrum/db/out.txt`, which the extension reads back. If the query fails, nothing arrives: the panel says so and the error is in the terminal. For MySQL there is no safe way to capture the output, so it runs in the terminal.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Anything that can destroy data (**DROP**, **TRUNCATE**, **ALTER**, or **UPDATE/DELETE with no WHERE**) shows the SQL and asks first.\n- The connection comes from your settings. A password inside a connection URL is typed in the terminal command: prefer a read-only database user, or a `.pgpass` file.\n- The settings cannot contain quotes, `$` or backticks.\n\nHandy commands: **List Tables**, **Describe a Table...**, **Show the First 20 Rows**, **Count Rows**.\n\n## Permissions\n\n**terminal**, **workspace.read** and **workspace.write** (for the two files in `.ferrum/db`).\n"}}}